{{also|wanze}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gmh|wanze}}, formed with the contractive suffix {{m|de|-ze}} (cf. {{m|de|Spatz}}, {{m|de|Heinz}}) from older Middle and {{der|de|goh|wantlūs|t=bug|lit=wall louse}}, equivalent to {{m|de|Wand}} + {{m|de|Laus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈvantsə/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Wanze.ogg|Audio}}
* {{rhymes|de|antsə|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|de|Wan|ze}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f}}

# an insect of the suborder '' {{taxfmt|Heteroptera|suborder}}'', a [[bug]] (in the strictest sense)
# {{lb|de|espionage}} [[bug]], [[wire]], [[wiretap]]
#: {{syn|de|Abhörgerät|Abhörwanze}}

